        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>End of 2004 and Welcome 2005!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									It has been a couple of months since our last update and during that time we have made some great progress.  The last update ended with us trying to get the Dust ring finished in Air and plotting to take on Xegony.  I'll take you guys through a few of our encounters..<BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Dec 4th - Dust Ring Mastered! Key to the last isle forged!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									We haven't been in the Plane of Air very long although it seemed like it.  We don't try encounters- fail and give up after one or even two tries then go do something else here at EoD.  Progression we take very seriously and our minds are totally focused on getting into Time.  Indeed our members although bored and frustrated trying/wiping/failing on scripts - such as the last ring for our PoA Xegony isle key - the famous 'Dust Ring' know that there is no alternative to get past this encounter. They know we must keep trying until it's done.  Sometimes people think that a change - perhaps a loot night - a night in Fire farming could be a nice change but the reality is that is an excuse to avoid repeating another tough night in Air.  Of course we feel that it is better to keep trying with blunt determination until we get it while its fresh in our minds.<BR><BR>This approach meantt Clan Dread went to Air Friday, Saturday, Wednesday and then the following Friday until finally with a collection of ideas and perfectly put into practice we broke the Dust ring in 30 minutes (in half the maximum time).  When the final spider went down and we triggered the main named of the ring a huge sigh of relief went through the raid and of course many joyful cheers.  This is the feeling many people play EQ for - it's the challenge of the event, the way we try to tackle the issues and then finally the way we overcome the problems - as a guild and with pure team work.<BR><BR>'Sigismond Windwalker' was up and targetable.  We pulled him over and engaged.  We were busy smashing him down quite happily even though his mem blur tactics were going off every other second.  There was much Wizard and Mage tanking while the tanks unloaded the nukes!  He died nevertheless and the Avatar of Dust was spawned! <BR><BR>We smashed The Avatar of Dust down and collected our final part to make the Xegony isle key!   All our hard work had paid off and now we could focus our attention on the Queen herself!<BR><BR>The Queen was up - and although it was late we did have a bit of a play around with 20 Clan or so - mostly just testing - making some notes - checking some ranges.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000978.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000978.JPG" width=392 height=210 id=i1></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000979.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000979.JPG" width=400 height=250 id=i2></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Dec 7th - Plane of Fire Mack - Fennin Owned!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Since we had obtained our Xegony isle key and the raid had been tortured the last four raid nights we thought it would be good to get some EP looting done.  Fennin was up so we decided to pay him a visit.  We didn't have a huge raid force - around 35 - but our 'Minimum Break' ideal told us we need to get Fennin down.  We didn't have the perfect set of classes either - couple of clerics and a few druids would do though.<BR><BR>We managed to obtain a new personal guild record of 35 Clan on Fennin in around 12 minutes of pure perfected mack -  a totally flawless kill.<BR><BR>We also hit some minis while in the area which is really just the icing on the cake of a reward for the hard work in PoAir.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000980.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000980.JPG" width=322 height=234 id=i3></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000981.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000981.JPG" width=368 height=239 id=i4></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Dec 9th - Cursed & Emperor - old mack!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Too much of one thing can be a bad thing.  Of course we are happily progressing in the EPs however some of our members are pining for a little of the old stuff.  We decided to do an optional Cursed and Emperor kill in Ssra Temple.  <BR><BR>Nothing fancy here - 36 Clan took out the Emp in the usual style then went back for Cursed.  <BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000677.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000677.JPG" width=497 height=114 id=i5></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000782.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000782.JPG" width=268 height=250 id=i6></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Mid December - Xegony Owned! 2 Down - 3 to go!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Since our obtaining the key we had a couple of attempts in Air on Xegony.  Our first try was really about handling the adds, getting positions right, getting the group tasks sorted out etc.  The second attempt we took her all the way down to  50% with around 41 Clan.   Indeed everyone was FM but Xegony's huge spikey damage just clipped our MT and we fell.  Still it was a great run - and we knew ourselves we could easily do her again with the same numbers.  Nothing really would change - we had the strat sorted out.<BR><BR>Our third attempt on Xegony - on the 18th December and only 3 weeks in Plane of Air we dropped Xegony like a bad habbit.  Pure perfection - flawless kill.  No bullshit just business.  We wanted our Air elemental Time part, we came, we macked and we took it.<BR><BR>We were now 2 gods down and 2 to go - although we can consider access to time 5 parts - Arbiter in Earth being a reasonable segment to the key.  With Xegony down we could focus our attention to the Plane of Earth!<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000982.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000982.JPG" width=377 height=194 id=i7></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000983.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000983.JPG" width=317 height=181 id=i8></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>19th Dec - Plane of Fire Farmage!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Totally cleared up PoF - all minis and Fennin Ro Script - entire thing in about five hours with around 40 Clan.   The mobs may as well just Fed-Ex the loot to our home towns - it's just that easy.   I know some guilds have problems killing some of these minis with less than 30 and to be honest I don't see why - for us - after we had a play and got to the know the mobs it instantly became routine to all - probably a pull every 10 minutes - sometimes so quick between minis we forget to let the MT get his disc back.<BR><BR>We picked up about 10 molds and five item drops - a perfect reward for the Xegony smack a day earlier!<BR><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>20th Dec - Vex Thal - Tax Collection!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Theres still a demand for some illusion and special clickie effect items from Vex.  Indeed it's a perfect place for new members just joining EoD to get their resists, FT and general stats up without too much competition from the older members.  Of course Aten still has some pretty decent drops too.<BR><BR>We cleared from the Zone in to Aten in around seven hours - which isn't great - but we only had 27.  Picked up 14-15 drops or so.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000984.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000984.JPG" width=388 height=207 id=i9></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000985.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000985.JPG" width=388 height=216 id=i10></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>21st Dec - Plane of Fire - More Farmage!  Agnarr backmack!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Cleared up fire again - all minis including Fennin.  Few more this time - around 50 members - the difference from 35 - 50 of course just makes it a little quicker - the  approach is the same however.<BR><BR>By the time we finished in Fire it was still pretty early and a couple of members needed an Agnarr flag for EP access so we headed over.  By that time we were left with 28 or so - still Agnarr died all the same.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000929.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000929.JPG" width=383 height=183 id=i11></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000986.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000986.JPG" width=385 height=216 id=i12></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>24th Dec - Plane of Earth Rings - Arbiter OWNED!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									With nearly everyone in the entire guild having Fennin and 80%+ having Xegony we now would focus our attention on the Plane of Earth.  We knew we had to get through some very long ring events to spawn the Arbiter and then defeat the Arbiter within a time period to get our PoEb (Stronghold of the Twelve) flag.  It would certinaly be a long night.<BR><BR>We'd been having some discussions lately with Wind of Tranquility regarding perhaps a one day a week alliance raid.  We had known WoT for a long while - both EoD and WoT are very old guilds to Antonius Bayle and we were on good terms.  WoT and EoD were now level pegging in EP terms so it seemed a good thing to do.  Neither guild had anything to prove regarding minimum break on various encounters - both could easily do the Earth rings alone - however it would be fun to team up and perhaps path the way to a future alliance on other mobs.<BR><BR>We set about clearing all the rings - which we did with reasonable pace.  Regardless of the pace - they still take a good amount of time each - longer with the Croc up.  Eventually we finished the rings and headed over for Arbiter.  We smashed him down with a good ten minutes to spare.<BR><BR>Clan Dread were now 3/5ths of the way to Time.  Fennin, Xegony, Arbiter down - now Rath and Coirnav remain - two encounters we were looking forward to.<BR><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>28th Dec - PoFire and Vex Thal Farming</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Seems to be a popular trend that every time we defeat a PoP GoD/Boss that gives us more progression into Time that we do a little loot farming to compensate.  They appear to be the perfect partner - and I don't think any members are complaining.  Fennin and Aten down again.<BR><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>1st Jan - Happy New Year Clan Dread!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									What a great year we've had.  We've progressed right the way through PoP and into EP.  We had some trying times - but we stuck at it and got the results!  Indeed in the last six months we've really accellerated.<BR><BR>Indeed when EQ2 and WoW were released in mid December a lot of guilds lost many members. For EoD we just got stronger.  I think some 3-4 guilds have joined up.  However our overall member count has risen quite sharply in December by around 20-30 people.<BR><BR>Things are looking good for us and we hope to keep up the great work (uber mack) and get through Time - in no time!<BR><BR><BR>WELL DONE ALL!<BR><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
